    "ls|LS16_S15_U_11": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.11 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.07.2018 \n \n \nGUIDELINES FOR STOPPAGE OF TRAINS \n \n †*11. SHRI  RAJU SHETTY: \n \n \n     Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n \n(a) whether his Ministry has received complaints from public \nrepresentatives and people during the last six -seven years regarding \nproviding stoppage of both Rani Chennamma and Haripriya Express \ngoing towards Tirupati from Kolhapur (Maharashtra) at Jaysingpur \nrailway station; \n \n(b)    if so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(c) whether the stoppage of both these trains at other stations has \nbeen provided as per the guidelines; and \n \n \n(d)  if so, the list of those stations as well as the guidelines \nprescribed by the Railways for provision of stoppage of trains? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COAL, FINANCE AND CORPORATE AFFAIRS \n \n    (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n \n (a) to (d):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n**** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 11 BY SHRI RAJU SHETTY TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 18.07.2018 REGARDING GUIDELINES \nFOR STOPPAGE OF TRAINS \n \n(a)  & (b) Yes, Madam.  Representations from the Hon’ble Members of \nParliament have been received for provision of stoppage of Rani \nChennamma Express and Haripriya Express at Jaysingpur. \n \n(c) & (d) Experimental stoppage of 17415/17416 Tirupati-Shri Chhatrapati \nShahu Maharaj(T) (Kohlapur) Haripriya Express has been provided at \nHatkanangale station w.e.f. 15 .11.2008 while that of 16589/16590 \nBengaluru-Shri Chhatrapati Shahu Maharaj(T) (Kolhapur) Rani \nChennamma Express has been provided at Dodbele w.e.f. 17.03.2016.  At \npresent, Indian Railways have a policy on stoppage of trains. Some of \nthe important criteria stipulated are as under:-  \n(i) Total sale of tickets at the station for both U p and Down \ndirections distance wise, class-wise & cost wise. \n(ii) Traffic pattern at the station. \n(iii) Availability of alternative services, convenience and occupancy \nof existing services. \n(iv) Nature of train and its occupancy. \n(v) Passing time of the train concerned at the station where \nstoppage is under consideration. \n(vi) Operational constraints viz. effect of stoppage on the line \ncapacity of the section and punctuality of other services \n \nThe policy guidelines which encompasses both the operational and \ncommercial aspects for provision of stoppage of trains inter alia  \nstipulate that the minimum number of ticke ts to be sold at the station \nso as to recover the cost of stoppage (which ranges from `12,716/- to    \n2/-  \n\n           \n-2- \n \n`24,506/- depending upon traction, composition and other factors) \nshould be 40 or more tickets per day per train for sleeper class for a \ndistance of 500 kms or its equivalent in terms of cost for mixed class \nof passengers like AC, General and distance (mult iple of 100 kms) \ntoward/from destination/originating stations of the train. The policy \nalso stipulates that no additional stoppage to be provided in sections \nhaving capacity utilization above 90%. Additionally, population and \nsignificance of the town/city and new developments, thereat, are \nother factors taken into account while considering provision of new \nstoppages. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S15_U_110": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 110 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.07.2018 \n \nVACANT POSTS \n \n110. SHRI ANTO ANTONY: \n \n   Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has issued notices for filling  up \nof various vacancies existing in Railways; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof including the number of posts, \nnumber of applications received and the present status of \nthe applications;  \n \n(c) whether it is true that the Government has received three \ncrore applications for 90000 vacancies; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n  \n \n \nANSWER \n \n \n      MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n***** \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 110 BY SHRI ANTO ANTONY  TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 18.07.2018 REGARDING VACANT \nPOSTS \n \n \n(a) to (d) Yes, Madam. The details are as under-  \n \nCentralized \nEmployment \nNotification \n(CEN) No. \nName of \nPost \nTotal \nnumber of \nnotified \nvacancies \nTotal \nnumber of \napplications \nreceived \n01/2018 \n \nAssistant \nLoco Pilot \n& \nTechnician \n26,502 47,55,920 \n02/2018 \nLevel-1 \n(erstwhile \nGroup ‘D’) \n62,907 1,89,78,913 \nTotal 89,409 2,37,34,833 \n \n       The scrutiny of the applications has been completed. \n  \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
