    "ls|LS16_S15_U_42": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.42\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 20TH JULY, 2018\nNATIONAL URBAN HEALTH MISSION\n*42. SHRI SANKAR PRASAD DATTA:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to\nstate:\n(a) whether all the State Governments have implemented the National Urban\nHealth Mission (NUHM);\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) if not, the names of the States which are yet to implement the same along with\nthe reasons therefor; and\n(d) the steps taken/being taken by the Union Government to ensure implementation\nof the Mission by all States and strengthen the primary health care system in cities\nand towns under the said Mission?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF  HEALTH AND\nFAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY)\n(a) to (d) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 42* FOR 20TH JULY, 2018\n(a) & (b) All the States/UTs are implementing the National Urban Health Mission\n(NUHM) except the UT of Lakshadweep.\n(c)  National Urban Health Mission (NUHM), as a sub -mission under an\noverarching National Health Mission (NHM), was approved on 1st May, 2013 fo r\nproviding equitable and quality primary health care services to the urban\npopulation with special focus on the slum and vulnerable population. NUHM\ncovers all cities, towns and District Headquarters with more than 30,000\npopulation.  The UT of Lakshadweep continues to be covered under National Rural\nHealth Mission (NRHM) as the population of the District Headquarter is less than\n30,000.\n(d) Since the launch of NUHM, an amount of Rs.4043.86 Crore has been released\ntill 1st Quarter of Financial Year 2018-19 to strengthen primary health care system\nin urban areas, particularly in the slums and its neighborhood.\nMinistry has also been providing continuous technical support and guidance\nto the States/UTs. Various guidelines, brochures on thematic areas have been\ndeveloped and shared with the States.  Training and capacity building is also being\nsupported besides regular team visits to the States.\n*****",
    "ls|LS16_S15_U_43": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 43 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.07.2018 \n \nPENDING RAILWAY PROJECTS IN KERALA \n \n43. SHRI MULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN: \n  \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken any review of the pending \nrailway projects in Kerala; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) the present status of such pending projects along with funds \nallocated and utilized in the last four years; and  \n(d) the details of measures taken by the Railways for early \nexecution of pending projects? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n (SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 43 BY SHRI MULLAPPALLY \nRAMACHANDRAN TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 18.07.2018 \nREGARDING PENDING RAILWAY PROJECTS IN KERALA \n \n(a) to (c): Reviewing of pending/ongoing projects is a continuous \nprocess taken up with the concerned authorities to assess \nimpediments affecting the projects and their mitigation to expedite \nprogress of the projects. Details of pending/ongoing projects falling \nfully/partly in Kerala alongwith their present status, funds allocated \nand expenditure incurred thereon during last four years between \nMarch 2014 and March 2018  are as under:- \n(` in crore) \nS. \nNo. \nProject Latest \nEstimated \ncost \nExpenditure  \nincurred \nduring last \nfour years \nOutlay \n2018-\n19 \nStatus \n NEW LINE     \n1. Tirunavaya-\nGuruvayur \n(35 Km) \n477 15.83 10 Government of Kerala \nhas approved alignment \nin 2009 and Final \nLocation Survey (FLS) for \nfirst 8 Km completed.  \nBalance FLS is held up \ndue to public protest.  \n2. Angamali-\nSabrimala \n(116 Km) \n2815.62 126.44 219.90 On this project, work on \nAngamali-Kaladi section \n(7 Km) is in advance \nstage which, how