    "ls|LS16_S15_U_75": "������������������� �\n������������������������ ��� ����������������������� �\n��������� �\n������������������������� �\n���������������������������� �\n�\n��������������������������������������� �\n�\n����� ����� ����� ������� ���������� �\n����� ������������� ������������ �������� �\n�\n����� ���� ��������� ��� ������������ ���� ������������ ����������� ���\n������������������\n�\n���� ����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������\n�\n���� ��������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� �����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������ �\n�\n� ��������������������� ����������������� �������������\n���������� �\n���������������������� �\n�\n�\n�������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������� ���������� ��� ������ �������� �������� �������� ���� ��� ���� ���������\n������������\n�\n�������\n� �\n\n�",
    "ls|LS16_S15_U_76": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.76\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.07.2018\nINDIANS STRANDED ABROAD\n76.     SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR:\n       Will the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n(a) the number of Indians stranded in foreign countries who have been\nrescued and brought back by the Indian Government;\n(b) the  different  measures  taken  in  achieving  the  above-mentioned\ngoal;\n(c) the details of the countries from which these Indians were brought\nback; and\n(d) the State-wise details of the rescued Indians?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)]\n(a) to (d) The Government of India has accorded the highest priority to\nensure  the  safety  and  well-being  of  Indian  nationals  abroad.  As  per\ninformation available in the Ministry, the number of Indians who were\nstranded in foreign countries, and have been rescued and brought back\nduring the period April 2014 to December 2017 by the Indian Government\nfrom countries affected by war, internal strife and natural disasters, is\n1,01,336.  This figure also includes repatriation of Indian nationals from\nabroad  for  various  other  reasons  including  those  caught  in  situations,\nimpacted by economic slowdown in the Gulf region and facing difficulty\ndue to employment related issues.  Details are given at Annexure.\n*****\n\nANNEXURE\nS.\n N\no.\nName of\nCountry\nNumber of persons \nwhom assistance was \nextended during May \n2014 to December \n2017 \nDomicile of individual\n1 Afghanistan 184 Maharashtra, West Bengal, \nTamil Nadu,  Delhi, Haryana, Telangana, Jammu\nand Kashmir, Jharkhand\n2 Algeria 81 Bihar, Kerala, Maharashtra, Odisha, Punjab,\nRajasthan\n3 Azerbaijan 45 Tamil Nadu, Maharashtra, West Bengal, Punjab,\nKarnataka, Rajasthan\n4 Bahrain 403 Maharashtra, Andhra Pradesh, Telangana,\nRajasthan, Delhi, Gujarat, Kerala\n5 Belarus 7 Punjab, Uttarakhand, Bihar\n6 Bangladesh 33 West Bengal, Andhra Pradesh, Delhi , Assam,\nBihar, Uttar Pradesh\n7 Brazil 1 Tamil Nadu\n8 Brunei 3 Kerala\n9 Cambodia 19 Kerala, Punjab, Tamil Nadu, West Bengal, Bihar,\nUttarakhand, Uttar Pradesh\n10 Canada 4 Uttar Pradesh, Maharashtra, Bihar\n11 China 47 Kerala, Punjab, Andhra Pradesh, Uttar Pradesh,\nGujarat, Rajasthan\n12 Colombia 14 Kerala, Uttar Pradesh, Punjab, Delhi, Haryana,\nRajasthan\n13 Congo 1 Andhra Pradesh \n14 Cote D’ Ivoire 7 Hyderabad, Tamil Nadu, Maharashtra, Kerala\n15 Cuba 1 Punjab\n16 Cyprus 4 Haryana, Delhi\n17 Denmark 12 Punjab, Andhra Pradesh\n18 Egypt 12 Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh\n19 Ethiopia 15 Gujarat, Haryana, Delhi, Punjab\n20 Fiji 6 Maharashtra, Punjab\n21 Germany 2 Haryana\n22 Ghana 33 Kerala, Uttar Pradesh, Maharashtra, Tamil Nadu\n23 Hungary 4 Punjab \n24 Indonesia 52 Punjab, Uttar Pradesh, Delhi,  Tamil Nadu,\nOrissa,\n25 Iran 162 Haryana, Gujarat, Assam, Punjab, Uttar Pradesh,\nTamil Nadu, Bihar, Delhi, Kerala\n26 Iraq 6664 Bihar, Uttar Pradesh, Telengana, Gujarat, Punjab,\nRajasthan, Haryana,Tamil Nadu, Orissa, West\nBengal\n27 Ireland 1 Karnataka\n28 Israel 11 Karnataka, Maharashtra, Uttar Pradesh,\nRajasthan, Punjab, Kerala\n29 Jamaica 6 Maharashtra, Haryana, Gujarat\n30 Jordan 86 Kerala, Uttarakhand, Tamil Nadu, Bihar, Uttar\nPradesh, Punjab, Gujarat, Orissa, Kerala\n\n31 Kenya 24 Punjab, Kerala, Uttarakhand, Uttar Pradesh,\nGujarat\n32 Korea (Republic\nof)\n18 Tamil Nadu, Uttarakhand, Orrisa, Punjab, Kerala,\nUttar Pradesh, \n33 Kuwait 12753 Andhra Pradesh, Telangana\n34 Lao PDR 16 Kerala\n35 Lebanon 12 Punjab, Haryana, Uttar Pradesh, Delhi\n36 Libya 1395 Punjab, Maharashtra, Kerala, Uttar Pradesh,\nAndhra Pradesh, Telangana, Rajasthan, Gujarat,\nHaryana, Bihar, Himachal Pradesh, Karnataka\n37 Madagascar 6 Gujarat\n38 Malawi 1 Tamil Nadu\n39 Malaysia 1747 Tamil Nadu, Kerala, Uttar Pradesh, Punjab,\nBihar, Andhra Pradesh, Haryana, Himachal\nPradesh, J&K\n40 Maldives 35 Tamil Nadu, Bihar, Andhra Prad